### Short read on “teachers + mobile” from this alone

- **`ensureDirectorBranches` does nothing for `teacher`** (early `return`), so teachers rely on **`/me` → `me.campuses` → `branch_ids` → `teacherBranches` → `ensureTeacherBranch()`**. If `me.campuses` is empty or IDs don’t intersect `branches`, **`ensureTeacherBranch` exits without changing `currentBranch`**, while **`onMounted` already set `currentBranch` from public `loadBranches()` / `localStorage`**.
- **Teacher `mobile-branch-bar` only renders when `teacherBranches.length > 0`**; otherwise there is no mobile branch UI even though `currentBranch` may still be set.
- **`SmartCalendar` for teachers does not require `branchId` for the early exit** (`!branchId && !isTeacher`), and uses **`teacher_id`** on API/Supabase when `isTeacher` — so a “blank calendar” for teachers is more likely **`userId`/token/API**, or **downstream pages** (e.g. `AttendancePage`) that might still require `branchId`, not this `loadCourses` guard alone.

If you want, a follow-up read-only pass can grep `AttendancePage.vue` for the same `branchId`/teacher pattern.

